# 2pc-lb 6, 7 (Table 2) and 2pc-lb-cb 6, 7 (Table 3): owner 2026-11-03 20:45; stateless after the stateful of the same instance
# 2pc-le = election ring conf 10 (Table 2) and 2pc-le-split = election ring split 11 (Table 3): owner 2026-11-03 21:05; no stateless row (ring conf 8 already timed out at 1 h) unless the owner asks
# 2pc-tr 8 bag (Table 2) and 2pc-tr-iav 8 bag (Table 3): owner 2026-11-03 21:20; bag stays if the stateful correct pair finishes within 48 h, else the tables switch to fifo; no stateless row (size 8 timed out at 1 h)
# chan 7 (Table 2) and chan-ns 7 (Table 3), owner 2026-11-03 22:10: exports and joins; the stateful runs of both pairs are running on brain01 (shared) and are not duplicated here; no stateless (chan 6 stateless already 2 025 s)
# ewd998 5 (Table 2) and ewd998-nb 5 (Table 3), owner 2026-11-03 22:20: size 4 (1 h timeouts so far) first at 48 h, size 5 behind it guarded by needok on the size-4 row of the same engine; no stateless (size 4 stateless timed out at 1 h)
# lb = rr against a4b (Table 2) and lb-strict = rr against a4a (Table 3), owner 2026-11-03 22:35: sizes 3,3,3 and 4,4,4; the a4b 4,4,4 rows are guarded by the a4b 3,3,3 stateful (33 M spec graphs); one impl export serves both joins; no stateless
# lock (fifo pair, Table 2) and lock-wr (wrong-round, Table 3) at 3,4 and 3,5, owner 2026-11-03 22:45: 3,5 timed out at 1 h on every engine, 3,4 took 13 min stateful; 3,4 is the fallback; no stateless (3,4 stateless timed out at 1 h)
# pbkv pb at 6,2 and 4,4 (Table 2), owner 2026-11-03 23:00: the 4,4 export exceeded 250 GB at the 1 h tier, so its offline cell is expected to be oom; no stateless (6,2 stateless timed out at 1 h)
# replog-co 5 fifo and ring-el 6 (Table 2), replog-co-er 5 fifo and ring-el-nc 6 (Table 3), owner 2026-11-03 23:10; stateless after the stateful (replog-co bag 5 stateless took 4.9 h at 48 h; ring-el 5 stateless 178 s)
# zab 4 (Table 2) and zab-issue1 4 (Table 3), owner 2026-11-03 23:20: the last application rows; stateless after the stateful (size 3 stateless 150 s)
# Order (owner, 2026-11-04 10:05): every stateful and offline row of every instance first; the stateless rows (needok on their stateful row) at the end
